# POOLER CAPACITY on the PLAIN SDIST arm.  WIDE: one hidden layer of 64.
# dataset=YouTube d_emb=64 k_train=5 lr=1e-3 seed=5 patience 8
# branch=exp/escape-instrumentation commit=44413a26 (DETACHED WORKTREE, pinned, clean tree)
# TEMPEST_POOL_FEAT=sdist  TEMPEST_POOL_LAYERS=1  --hidden-dim 64
#
# QUESTION. Plain sdist (age, pos, dist(seed,token)) never escapes: it grinds to
#   val 0.4451 / test 0.4002 and stops, while the rad control jumps at ep14-15 to
#   0.5590-0.5626.  Phase 1 measured the mechanism: at the escape the pooler
#   briefly DIFFUSES (pool_eff 5.87 -> 7.53 over ep13-15, leading val by two
#   epochs), dE peaks, link decay re-accelerates from -6%/ep to -27%/ep, then
#   pool_eff settles at 5.42 -- tighter than the pre-escape floor.  Under sdist
#   pool_eff never leaves 5.20-5.67; the transient does not happen at all.
#
#   Is that a CAPACITY limit of the 161-param pooler, or a property of the
#   feature?  These two arms give the pooler more room without touching its
#   inputs.  wide64 = Linear(3,64)-GELU-Linear(64,1), 321 params.
#   deep2 = Linear(3,32)-GELU-Linear(32,32)-GELU-Linear(32,1), 1217 params.
#
# NO INIT CONFOUND ON E. E is drawn before the pooler, so all three arms share
#   a bit-identical embedding table (sha1 c4641d510d331f16 at n=2000,d=64,seed 5);
#   only the pooler weights differ (161/321/1217 params, hashes 791d4bae /
#   f2d7552 / e3f6df79).  A pooler-only init draw does differ between arms, so a
#   gap under ~0.01 is not separable from init luck -- but the escape is +0.17,
#   two orders of magnitude clear of that.
#
# READ pool_eff AT ep13-15, NOT THE FINAL MRR. If capacity was the binding
#   constraint, pool_eff lifts off ~6 toward ~7.5 there and val follows two
#   epochs later.  If it stays pinned near 5.2-5.7 through ep18, capacity is not
#   the constraint and the feature is.
#
# REFERENCE (same dataset/config/seed): rad control test 0.5590 (peak 0.5626),
#   escape ep14-15.  Plain sdist val 0.4451 / test 0.4002, stop ep24, no escape.
#
# Both arms run CONCURRENTLY on the single GPU, so wall-clock per epoch is ~1.5-2x
#   the solo figure; that affects timing only, not the numbers.
# started=2026-09-17 02:37:26
